        "title": "Connectedness",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nDEFINITION: X is CONNECTED if it cannot be written as X = U ∪ V where\n  U, V are disjoint, nonempty, and open."
    },
    {
      "id": "05-CONNECTEDNESS.md#006",
      "path": [
        "05-CONNECTEDNESS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:topology:05-connectedness, git-history:topology:05-connectedness]",
        "canonical_path": "topology/05-CONNECTEDNESS.md",
        "concepts": "[connectedness]",
        "current_path": "topology/05-CONNECTEDNESS.md",
        "id": "maxim:topology:connectedness",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "topology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[connectedness]",
        "section": "topology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Connectedness",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "EQUIVALENCES:\n  X is connected iff:\n  - The only clopen (closed-and-open) sets are ∅ and X.\n  - Every continuous function f: X → {0,1} (discrete) is constant."
    },
